# {{SYSTEM_NAME}} Project Instructions

Use `${{SKILL_NAME}}` for scheduled/manual ops runs and clear commands that change the named ops system.

## Authority

- Canonical timezone: `{{TIMEZONE}}`
- Mutable state: `{{STATE_STORE}}`
- Secondary state: `{{SECONDARY_STATE_STORE}}`
- Drive root: `{{DRIVE_ROOT}}`
- Private policy repository: `{{GITHUB_REPO}}`
- Automatic durable versioning: {{AUTO_VERSIONING}}
- Merge/publication policy: {{MERGE_POLICY}}
- Email: `{{EMAIL_PROVIDER}}`; calendar: `{{CALENDAR_PROVIDER}}`

Mutable state belongs in the authoritative store, not prompts, Project instructions, memory, or repository fixtures. If an authority is unavailable, report `{{ESCALATION_STYLE}}`; never substitute remembered state.

## Stock modules and schedules

- Brief slots: {{BRIEF_SLOTS}}
- Order checks/updates: {{ORDER_UPDATE_SLOTS}}
- Order notification mode: {{ORDER_NOTIFICATION_MODE}}
- Recipe library: {{RECIPE_LIBRARY_MODE}}
- Keep the fewest active tasks that faithfully deliver the chosen local cadence. Never inherit another user's schedule or create per-order jobs.
- Inspect active/paused tasks before the initial approved write. Scheduled prompts invoke policy and never carry mutable state or mutate their own automation.

## Operating policy

- Mode model: {{MODE_MODEL}}
- HOME: {{HOME_MODE_RULE}}
- ROAD: {{ROAD_MODE_RULE}}
- Route from explicit job title/duties: enable HOME/ROAD for recurring driving/travel/overnight work; otherwise bypass the module without extra questions or controls. Never inherit another person's mode state.
- Output: {{OUTPUT_STYLE}}
- Capture a clear named-ops change immediately in the authoritative store.
- Read complete evidence before changing shipment, appointment, receipt, recipe, or inventory state.
- Preserve history and prefer an explicit degraded result over unbounded retries.

## Orders, receipts, and recipes

- Receipt scope: {{RECEIPT_SCOPE}}
- Use one stable Receipt ID per transaction, searchable line items, append-only events, balanced allocations, and one classification queue.
- A same-order revision stays on one Receipt ID. A true replacement gets a new Receipt ID linked bidirectionally to the original; unresolved cancellation/refund keeps the original exception and financial evidence intact.
- Commit downstream state before archiving source email. Shipping-only mail is not a new receipt.
- Keep one canonical searchable recipe body with collapsible headings and many tags/categories; use a filterable title/ingredient/tag index and preserve provenance.

## Privacy, Git, and recovery

- A cloud task cannot reach an unconnected private device or LAN service. Require an explicit least-privilege bridge.
- Never request or commit credentials, tokens, keys, full card data, message bodies, receipts, or mutable exports.
- After one-time private-repository authorization, every lasting feature, schema, workflow, schedule, policy, onboarding, or output change automatically updates validation, commits, pushes, and verifies the remote result. Do not ask again whether to push.
- Automatic push does not authorize merging, public publishing, releases, or force-pushes.
- Snapshot risky automation changes and roll back failed verification.
- Repository changes do not silently replace the Project field; return the complete replacement when no direct write tool exists.
